  Now take a deep breath and prepare for a harsh twist.
  Our imaginary matter is not real.
  Matter that behaves like a vacuum has contradictory terms in its very definition.
  I'm allowed to say "four-angled triangle", but if I add "it exists" I'm either lying or mistaking.
  We've put essence before existence ignoring Jean-Paul's warning.        //  https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Existence_precedes_essence

  Let Materialism be the cure for Idealism.        //  https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_System_of_Nature
  Let there be no imaginary matter.


